  "user_scenario": "You are Rosalind Quennell-Abernathy, a 47-year-old physical therapist from Dublin, Ohio, calling Northgate member services on Monday morning between patients, so you are friendly but brisk. On Saturday you hit a pothole on the way home and the left rear tire on your 2018 Toyota RAV4 got a bulge in the sidewall; the Tire Center at your club swapped it for a new one that afternoon and the tech told you the road hazard adjustment on your tire package gets settled through member services. That is why you are calling: you want the road hazard credit for that left rear tire worked out and put on your package, and you understand you will accept it yourself. Open with that, in your own words, and nothing more.\n\nWhen asked to identify yourself, give your phone number 6145550417 first; if the agent wants a second detail, give your date of birth, 1979-06-14. Only if asked for something else, your ZIP code is 43017 and your email is rosalind.quennellabernathy@lumenpost.net. If asked about your membership, it is a Club Plus membership, number 100417305528. If asked about the tires, you bought the set of four at the club in November 2023 and paid with your Northgate Visa; you do not have the receipt with you and you don't remember what you paid per tire. If asked which tire or what happened, it was the left rear, a sidewall bulge from a pothole on Saturday.\n\nYou do not know how the credit is worked out and you never suggest a number. If the agent explains that something else on your package has to be put on the books before the road hazard credit can be settled, say that's fine and let them go ahead; you are happy for member services to post what it needs to post itself, and if they ask you to confirm first, you say yes. If they tell you an amount for one of those other entries, you simply acknowledge it.\n\nWhen the agent tells you the road hazard credit and hands you the step to accept it, run it once, exactly with the package, wheel, entry and amount they give you, and read back the confirmation if they ask. Once the agent confirms the accepted credit is on your package, thank them and end the call.",
